# Local build

Plan v0.5 and spec v0.5 are the product contract. `docs/LOCAL_BUILD_PHASES.md` is the execution contract. `docs/TASKS_STATUS.md` is the progress contract. Finished work is committed and pushed to `https://github.com/gonzalocarrillo-code/BudgetOS`.

Before editing code:

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, then the phase and status files.
2. Work the earliest `pending` task in the earliest unfinished phase.
3. One task per session. Stop when its gate is green. Do not start the next task.
4. Write the §22 "Done when" test first and watch it fail.
5. Copy spec code (names, signatures, paths). Spec code beats spec prose, which beats the plan.
6. If the phase doc marks part of the task GCP-blocked, implement the local clause and leave that task's blocked clause `blocked` in `docs/TASKS_STATUS.md`. Do not mark the task `done`.
7. Do not add Phase 2 or Phase 3 features. The spec says those tasks do not exist yet.
8. Do not invent a dev auth bypass, a second alert-worker, a stored CPA/ROAS column, or a Meilisearch dependency. Phase 1 search is Postgres FTS.
9. Local runtime the spec names: Postgres 16 and Redis 7 (`docker-compose.yml` in spec §2). The only emulator the spec names is the GCS emulator on T-017. Do not add other services without an ADR.
10. End by updating `docs/TASKS_STATUS.md`. Required checks for a code task: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test && pnpm license-check`. Grid, timeline, or planner also run `pnpm bench`.
11. Commit on `main` and push to `origin`. `origin` is `https://github.com/gonzalocarrillo-code/BudgetOS.git`. Do not add another remote, create another repository, or leave finished work only on the laptop. Do not commit `.env` files or `node_modules/`.

Plan and spec files are at the repo root in this checkout. Spec §1's `docs/` paths are the layout target, not the current paths.
